& [Threats]
  + [T01] forged or drifted B2B1 receipt creates false rollback basis
  + [T02] live or non-disposable root is relabelled as a fixture
  + [T03] recovery owner is substituted or collapsed into activation authority
  + [T04] supplied trigger is laundered as observed boot failure
  + [T05] unsupported trigger widens P0
  + [T06] registry changed after B2B1 and rollback overwrites a third state
  + [T07] current registry bytes parse but differ from exact B2B1 successor bytes
  + [T08] predecessor source is missing tampered normalized linked or reparsed
  + [T09] failed candidate is deleted modified or treated as cleanup-authorized
  + [T10] restored generation rewinds or reuses an old snapshot identity
  + [T11] temp already exists or escapes the final parent
  + [T12] pre-replacement fault deletes a non-owned file
  + [T13] post-replacement durability fault is reported as atomic refusal or success
  + [T14] Windows Access Denied is bypassed with unsafe or weakened durability
  + [T15] receipt claims boot activation provider model process network or cleanup
  + [T16] unknown or oversized machine form bypasses strict parsing
  + [T17] evidence manifest admits duplicate nonportable linked or stale artifacts
  + [T18] rollback module imports live repository Git remote SWA-05 FPGA Minecraft or foreign authority
  + [T19] hostile concurrent writer races between observation and replacement

& [Controls]
  + T01 through T08 strict nested replay physical byte identity closed trigger exact owner and no-follow path checks
  + T09 explicit preservation flags and no cleanup surface
  + T10 monotonic generation distinct identities and digest replay
  + T11 through T14 B2B1 path protocol create_new owned-temp state and typed post-replacement refusal
  + T15 through T18 strict receipt nonclaims static forbidden-surface checks and physical evidence rehashing

& [Residual]
  + T19 remains outside P0 and prevents live-root use
  + boot semantic truth and operator consent remain outside and prevent activation claims

